<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">Frequently Asked Questions - Trademark Hearing in Pune</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Answers about trademark hearing triggers, preparation, virtual hearings, objection grounds, outcomes, timelines, and appeal options for Pune applicants.</p>
                    @include('partials.bigin-form', [
                        'variant'  => 'compact',
                        'service'  => 'Trademark Hearing in Pune',
                        'city'     => 'Pune',
                    ])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is a trademark hearing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>A trademark hearing (show cause hearing) is a formal proceeding where the applicant appears before the Hearing Officer at the Trademark Registry to defend their application against objections not resolved through the written reply to the examination report. It is the last opportunity before the Registrar accepts or refuses the application.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">When does a trademark hearing happen?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>When the Examiner issues a show cause hearing notice after finding the applicant's written reply unsatisfactory. IP India portal shows 'Ready for Show Cause Hearing'. Common triggers: Section 9 (descriptiveness, lack of distinctiveness) or Section 11 (similarity with existing marks). Notice ~15 days before hearing.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How to prepare for trademark hearing in Pune?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Analyse examination report objections (S.9 and/or S.11), research case law and precedents, compile usage evidence (invoices, advertising, sales, GST returns), prepare affidavit of usage, draft written submissions, arrange representation at TM Registry Mumbai (physical or virtual). Patron handles all from Pune.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What are the grounds for trademark objection?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Section 9 (absolute grounds): lack of distinctiveness, descriptive of goods/services, generic term, deceptive, contrary to public order. Section 11 (relative grounds): identical or confusingly similar to an earlier registered or pending mark for same/similar goods/services.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I attend a trademark hearing virtually?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. Since 2020, TM Registry conducts hearings via video conference. Pune applicants attend virtually without travelling to TM Registry Mumbai. Need stable internet, working audio/video, screen-sharing capability, and all documents accessible digitally. Patron manages all virtual hearing logistics.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if I miss the trademark hearing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>The Hearing Officer may refuse or abandon your application at their discretion. Missing the hearing is one of the most common reasons applicants lose trademark rights. Patron monitors all client applications for hearing notices and ensures attendance - physical or virtual.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does it take to get a decision after hearing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Hearing Officer typically issues order within 2-8 weeks. If accepted: TM Journal publication in 2-4 weeks, then 4-month opposition period, then certificate in 2-4 weeks. Total from hearing to certificate: approximately 6-9 months if no opposition is filed.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-8">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the difference between trademark objection and hearing?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Objection is the written examination report citing refusal grounds. Objection reply is the applicant's written response (due within 30 days). Hearing is the formal oral proceeding that happens only if the Examiner is unsatisfied with the reply. The hearing is the escalation - the last chance to defend in person.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


            <!-- Quick Answers -->
            <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:32px;">
                <p><strong>Quick Answers</strong></p>
                <p><strong>Trademark hearing kab hota hai?</strong> Jab examination report ka reply Examiner ko satisfy nahi karta, tab show cause hearing notice aata hai. IP India pe 'Ready for Show Cause Hearing' status dikhta hai. TM Registry Mumbai mein hoti hai - physical ya virtual.</p><p><strong>Hearing miss kar diya to kya hoga?</strong> Application refuse ya abandon ho sakta hai. Trademark ka haq kho sakte ho. Hearing zaroor attend karo.</p><p><strong>Virtual hearing kaise hoti hai?</strong> 2020 se TM Registry video conference pe hearing karti hai. Internet, camera, mic chahiye. Patron setup karta hai test call ke saath.</p>

